WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.557 --> 00:00:02.417
- [Narrator] We're all
familiar with Coca-Cola.

00:00:02.417 --> 00:00:04.423
But this is also Coke.

00:00:04.423 --> 00:00:06.701
It's said that clear Coke
was a top secret project

00:00:06.701 --> 00:00:11.002
made exclusively for
a thirsty Red Russian.

00:00:11.002 --> 00:00:13.502
(light music)

00:00:15.316 --> 00:00:16.797
- Ah, so good.

00:00:16.797 --> 00:00:17.795
- [Narrator] During World War II,

00:00:17.795 --> 00:00:19.635
Coca-Cola made a global splash,

00:00:19.635 --> 00:00:21.736
boosting American troops' morale.

00:00:21.736 --> 00:00:25.197
At one point, Dwight D.
Eisenhower met with Georgy Zhukov,

00:00:25.197 --> 00:00:27.496
a Soviet general
instrumental in the defeat

00:00:27.496 --> 00:00:28.329
of Nazi Germany.

00:00:28.329 --> 00:00:29.909
(explosion)

00:00:29.909 --> 00:00:31.653
Eisenhower introduced him to Coke.

00:00:31.653 --> 00:00:32.490
- [Eisenhower] Try this.

00:00:32.490 --> 00:00:33.925
- [Narrator] Zhukov was hooked.

00:00:33.925 --> 00:00:35.747
But after the war, Coke
was seen as a symbol

00:00:35.747 --> 00:00:37.493
of American imperialism

00:00:37.493 --> 00:00:39.413
and was banned from the Soviet Union.

00:00:39.413 --> 00:00:40.906
Yeah, nope, not here.

00:00:40.906 --> 00:00:42.410
So Zhukov called up none other

00:00:42.410 --> 00:00:44.250
than U.S. president Harry Truman

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:46.133
to send him a secret stash.

00:00:46.133 --> 00:00:48.335
- [Zhukov] I'm gonna need Coca-Cola.

00:00:48.335 --> 00:00:50.533
- [Narrator] Truman
agreed to help Zhukov out.

00:00:50.533 --> 00:00:52.474
- [Truman] Alright, you got it.

00:00:52.474 --> 00:00:53.994
- [Narrator] He got the
top dogs at Coca-Cola

00:00:53.994 --> 00:00:56.037
to disguise its iconic look.

00:00:56.037 --> 00:00:57.957
They eliminated the
drink's artificial coloring,

00:00:57.957 --> 00:01:00.133
but made sure the new vodka look alike

00:01:00.133 --> 00:01:02.517
still had that classic Coke taste.

00:01:02.517 --> 00:01:04.714
They packaged it in
straight glass bottles,

00:01:04.714 --> 00:01:06.634
capped with a red star.

00:01:06.634 --> 00:01:08.394
According to a World War II Coke rep,

00:01:08.394 --> 00:01:11.008
50 cases were sent to Russia.

00:01:11.008 --> 00:01:12.874
Zhukov got his fix.

00:01:12.874 --> 00:01:14.474
He was never caught
with the disguised Cola,

00:01:14.474 --> 00:01:15.877
and as far as we know,

00:01:15.877 --> 00:01:17.909
it hasn't been sipped since.

00:01:17.909 --> 00:01:20.742
(laid back music)

